WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:15.330
That night Tom dreamed vividly about the haunted house adventure.

2
00:00:15.331 --> 00:00:18.794
The next morning he wasn't sure whether it had really happened.

3
00:00:18.795 --> 00:00:27.073
It seemed amazing that Injun Joe hadn't killed them, and it seemed just as amazing that ten-thousand dollars was hidden in the haunted house.

4
00:00:27.074 --> 00:00:29.895
After breakfast Tom went into town.

5
00:00:29.896 --> 00:00:33.604
He saw Huck fishing by the ferry landing.

6
00:00:33.605 --> 00:00:40.239
"Oh, Tom, if we hadn't brought our tools into that house, we'd be rich right now!" cried Huck sadly.

7
00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:46.915
"So it wasn't a dream!" said Tom. "I thought maybe I made it all up!"

8
00:00:46.916 --> 00:00:50.558
"We've got to find that money," he went on.

9
00:00:50.559 --> 00:00:53.533
"I don't know." Huck wasn't so sure.

10
00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:57.164
"A man has but one chance in a lifetime to make it rich.

11
00:00:57.165 --> 00:01:00.730
We had our chance, and we lost it, Tom," he said.

12
00:01:00.731 --> 00:01:07.139
"We know Injun Joe is going to hide the loot in 'number two under the cross,'" said Tom.

13
00:01:07.140 --> 00:01:11.294
"We've just got to figure out where number two is."

14
00:01:11.295 --> 00:01:14.339
"It could be a house number." said Huck.

15
00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:17.589
"Not in this town," said Tom.

16
00:01:17.590 --> 00:01:20.583
"Tavern rooms have numbers," said Huck.

17
00:01:20.584 --> 00:01:23.367
"I didn't know that," said Tom.

18
00:01:23.368 --> 00:01:26.966
"Hey, there are only two taverns in this town.

19
00:01:26.967 --> 00:01:32.414
You stay here, and I'll be back quick."

20
00:01:32.415 --> 00:01:36.405
When Tom returned, he told Huck what he had learned.

21
00:01:36.406 --> 00:01:41.068
"In the first tavern, room number two is rented by a young lawyer.

22
00:01:41.069 --> 00:01:46.488
In the other tavern, the tavern owner's son said room number two is a mystery.

23
00:01:46.489 --> 00:01:51.800
People only go in there at night, and it's always kept locked."

24
00:01:51.801 --> 00:01:55.236
"That's got to be the number two we're after," said Huck.

25
00:01:55.237 --> 00:01:58.629
"Somebody has to watch that room," said Tom.

26
00:01:58.630 --> 00:02:01.848
"There's a back door that goes out into the alley.

27
00:02:01.849 --> 00:02:05.262
That must be how Injun Joe comes and goes.

28
00:02:05.263 --> 00:02:08.497
You will be the one to watch the back door, Huck.

29
00:02:08.498 --> 00:02:12.368
People will know something is up if I do it."

30
00:02:12.369 --> 00:02:17.059
Huck still looked uncertain, but Tom finally talked him into watching the door.

31
00:02:17.060 --> 00:02:22.329
Tom said that if Huck watched the room, Tom could go into the tavern and look for the money.

32
00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:27.759
That seemed to satisfy Huck, and the boys parted with a handshake.

33
00:02:27.760 --> 00:02:30.975
After sunset the boys met again in back of the tavern.

34
00:02:30.976 --> 00:02:35.322
They were hoping for a cloudy night, but instead the night was clear.

35
00:02:35.323 --> 00:02:39.494
The moon was too bright for Tom to sneak into the room without being seen.

36
00:02:39.495 --> 00:02:42.995
He told Huck to keep an eye on the place.

37
00:02:42.996 --> 00:02:47.599
The next few nights remained clear, so Tom went home while Huck watched.

38
00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:52.747
Finally, on Thursday night, clouds covered the moon.

39
00:02:52.748 --> 00:02:59.170
All week Huck had seen no one coming or going, so just after midnight Tom sneaked into the tavern.

40
00:02:59.171 --> 00:03:01.941
He went quietly up the stairs to the door.

41
00:03:01.942 --> 00:03:05.572
Huck tried hard to watch him, but the night was too dark.

42
00:03:05.573 --> 00:03:08.816
It was as if Tom had been swallowed by the night.

43
00:03:08.817 --> 00:03:15.840
Suddenly Tom screamed, "Run for your life!" and he jumped over the railing of the stairs.

44
00:03:15.841 --> 00:03:19.249
Huck and Tom ran until they could hardly breathe.

45
00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:23.179
"Wh . . . what did you see?" gasped Huck.

46
00:03:23.180 --> 00:03:28.682
"I nearly stepped on Injun Joe's hand," said Tom, panting.

47
00:03:28.683 --> 00:03:32.181
Huck just stared at Tom, too scared to speak.

48
00:03:32.182 --> 00:03:35.244
"He was on the floor, with his hands spread out.

49
00:03:35.245 --> 00:03:39.441
There was an empty bottle and a cup near his head."

50
00:03:39.442 --> 00:03:43.196
"He was drunk?" asked Huck. Tom nodded.

51
00:03:43.197 --> 00:03:46.106
"Did you see the box?" continued Huck.

52
00:03:46.107 --> 00:03:50.986
Tom shook his head and said, "There was no time. I just ran.

53
00:03:50.987 --> 00:03:54.039
I didn't see the box, and I didn't see the cross.

54
00:03:54.040 --> 00:03:57.185
But I did see lots of barrels and bottles.

55
00:03:57.186 --> 00:04:01.937
I know the secret of that room—it's full of whiskey."

56
00:04:01.938 --> 00:04:09.471
Huck thought about that for a moment and said, "You know, Tom, if Injun Joe is drunk, this would be a good time to get the box."

57
00:04:09.472 --> 00:04:13.386
"All right," said Tom, "you try!"

58
00:04:13.387 --> 00:04:14.986
Huck shook his head.

59
00:04:14.987 --> 00:04:19.004
"You said there was only one empty bottle by his head. That isn't enough.

60
00:04:19.005 --> 00:04:22.631
If there were three bottles, then maybe I'd do it."

61
00:04:22.632 --> 00:04:27.407
"Well, there is one good thing that's come of this," said Tom.

62
00:04:27.408 --> 00:04:30.055
"We know where Injun Joe is.

63
00:04:30.056 --> 00:04:35.720
Now we just need to wait for him to leave, and we'll get in that room and search it properly."

64
00:04:35.721 --> 00:04:39.758
Huck agreed to keep watch all night and sleep during the day.

65
00:04:39.759 --> 00:04:45.231
"We'll get this money yet," he told Tom confidently.
